WitOS starts a dynamic program as a static one: its creator maps it and its interpreter, builds the Linux stack image and sends the process's capabilities (the kernel log and the boot package) in a start message on the channel endpoint the auxiliary vector names (witos/start.h). The dynamic linker opens libraries and may write a diagnostic before the program's own startup runs, so its third stage takes the start message first, as rcrt1.c does for a static program before __libc_start_main.

